        ("CSS Variables", "Declaring Custom Properties", "How do you declare and access a CSS Custom Property (Variable)?", "Declare with double dashes (--primary-color: #0284c7) and access with var(--primary-color).", "Easy", "Practical", ":root { --brand: #38bdf8; }\n.btn { background: var(--brand); }", "Can CSS variables have fallback values?"),
        ("CSS Variables", "Fallback in var()", "How do you provide a fallback value if a CSS variable is undefined?", "Pass the fallback as the second parameter: var(--custom-color, #1e293b).", "Easy", "Practical", "color: var(--text-color, #333333);", "Can a fallback be another var()?"),
        ("CSS Variables", "Scoping of Variables", "How does scoping work with CSS Variables?", "CSS variables follow normal inheritance and cascade: a variable declared on a class overrides the :root variable for that component and all its children.", "Intermediate", "Concept", ".theme-light { --bg: #fff; }\n.theme-dark { --bg: #000; }", "Can JavaScript update CSS variables dynamically?"),
        ("CSS Variables", "Updating CSS Variables via JS", "How do you update a CSS variable dynamically using JavaScript?", "document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--brand-color', '#3b82f6');.", "Easy", "Practical", "document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--theme', 'dark');", "Does updating a root variable trigger a repaint across all consumers?"),
        ("CSS Variables", "CSS Variables vs SASS Variables", "What is the major advantage of CSS custom properties over SASS ($variable)?", "CSS variables are live in the browser DOM, dynamically updatable in real time via JavaScript and media queries, and inherit through elements. SASS variables are compile-time constants.", "Intermediate", "Comparison", "", "Can SASS variables change on screen resize without compiling?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "CSS Nesting", "What is native CSS nesting and how is the '&' used?", "Modern CSS allows nesting child rules inside parent rules directly. '&' references the parent selector.", "Intermediate", "Practical", ".card {\n  background: white;\n  &:hover { background: #f8fafc; }\n  & .title { color: #0f172a; }\n}", "Is preprocessor nesting still required?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "Color Functions", "What is the advantage of hsl() and modern oklch() color formats in CSS?", "hsl and oklch represent colors intuitively (Hue, Saturation, Lightness / Perceptual Chroma). oklch ensures uniform perceived brightness across all hues.", "Intermediate", "Concept", "background: oklch(0.6 0.25 140);", "Why is rgb harder to manipulate programmatically?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "color-mix() Function", "What does color-mix(in srgb, red 40%, blue) do?", "It dynamically mixes two colors together in the specified color space in pure CSS without preprocessors.", "Advanced", "Practical", "background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--brand) 20%, transparent);", "How does this simplify alpha transparency?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "accent-color Property", "What does the accent-color property do on native form inputs?", "accent-color customizes the tint color of native checkboxes, radio buttons, range sliders, and progress bars with a single line.", "Easy", "Practical", ":root { accent-color: #38bdf8; }", "Does accent-color work on normal buttons?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "scrollbar-width and scrollbar-color", "How do you style scrollbars in modern standard CSS?", "Use scrollbar-width (auto, thin, none) and scrollbar-color (thumb-color track-color).", "Intermediate", "Practical", "html { scrollbar-width: thin; scrollbar-color: #555 #111; }", "What was the legacy WebKit scrollbar syntax?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "Responsive MCQ", "Which unit scales with user font settings in browser preferences?", "Option A is correct. rem scales relative to root font size.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "rem", "B": "px", "C": "vh", "D": "pt"}, "A", "What does em scale with?"),
        ("Modern CSS", "Animation MCQ", "Which property keeps the final frame styles after a CSS animation finishes?", "Option B is correct. animation-fill-mode: forwards keeps end styles.", "Easy", "MCQ", "", {"A": "animation-iteration-count: infinite", "B": "animation-fill-mode: forwards", "C": "animation-direction: alternate", "D": "animation-play-state: running"}, "B", "What does backwards do?"),
